From e2c728c84ae38808f2b67f12317f854ef9829c55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola <francesco-stimola@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:59:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] nouveau: pick the vc1 microcode for each picture type

nouveau loads vuc-vc1-0 for every VC-1 picture. NVIDIA's driver loads
vuc-vc1-1 for fields and vuc-vc1-2 for interlaced frames: with the
progressive one, VP decodes the second field of a frame wrongly, and the
frames after it too, and a stream mixing fields with interlaced frames
hangs it.

Load all three and pick one for each picture. Where this is untested (VP3
and VP5) or vuc-vc1-1 or 2 is missing, refuse interlaced pictures instead,
so that end_frame fails and the application can fall back to software
decoding.

Tested on a GeForce GT 240M (VP4) with FFmpeg's interlaced VC-1 streams:
SA10143 and ilaced_twomv now match software decoding, with no GPU errors
(ilaced_twomv, 1080 lines high, also needs 0018). MrNoname3 got the same
results with Mesa main on a GeForce 210 and on a GeForce GT 520M (Fermi,
nvc0 code). With vuc-vc1-1 missing or unreadable, interlaced pictures are
refused as before. Progressive VC-1, H.264 and MPEG-2 decode as before.
